{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type TaggedCustomEvent<T> = \n  | StructuredOutputStartEvent\n  | StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>\n  | ApprovalRequestedEvent\n  | ToolInputAvailableEvent;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1924","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:1924"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discriminated union of the orchestrator-tagged "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" events. Each variant\nhas a literal "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":", so a single narrow on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.name"},{"type":"text","value":" yields a typed\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" with no helper or cast:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'approval-requested') {\n  chunk.value.toolCallId // typed as string\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StructuredOutputCompleteEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" value is parameterized by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":", which\nthe chat orchestrator narrows to the schema's inferred type after Standard\nSchema validation. Adapters always emit it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T = unknown"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Caveat: tools can emit arbitrary user-defined custom events via the\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent(name, value)"},{"type":"text","value":" context API. Those flow through the stream\nat runtime but are intentionally absent from this union — including a bare\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":" (whose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value: any"},{"type":"text","value":" would poison the union) would collapse\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chunk.value"},{"type":"text","value":" back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":" after the narrow. If you rely on\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"emitCustomEvent"},{"type":"text","value":", branch on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" outside the literal-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" narrows\nor cast the chunk to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" to recover the wider shape."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype TaggedCustomEvent<T> = \n  | StructuredOutputStartEvent\n  | StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>\n  | ApprovalRequestedEvent\n  | ToolInputAvailableEvent;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1924](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1924)\n\nDiscriminated union of the orchestrator-tagged `CUSTOM` events. Each variant\nhas a literal `name`, so a single narrow on `chunk.name` yields a typed\n`value` with no helper or cast:\n\n```ts\nif (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'approval-requested') {\n  chunk.value.toolCallId // typed as string\n}\n```\n\nThe `StructuredOutputCompleteEvent` value is parameterized by `T`, which\nthe chat orchestrator narrows to the schema's inferred type after Standard\nSchema validation. Adapters always emit it with `T = unknown`.\n\nCaveat: tools can emit arbitrary user-defined custom events via the\n`emitCustomEvent(name, value)` context API. Those flow through the stream\nat runtime but are intentionally absent from this union — including a bare\n`CustomEvent` (whose `value: any` would poison the union) would collapse\n`chunk.value` back to `any` after the narrow. If you rely on\n`emitCustomEvent`, branch on `CUSTOM` outside the literal-`name` narrows\nor cast the chunk to `StreamChunk` to recover the wider shape.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` = `unknown`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: TaggedCustomEvent\ntitle: TaggedCustomEvent\n---\n\n```ts\ntype TaggedCustomEvent<T> = \n  | StructuredOutputStartEvent\n  | StructuredOutputCompleteEvent<T>\n  | ApprovalRequestedEvent\n  | ToolInputAvailableEvent;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:1924](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L1924)\n\nDiscriminated union of the orchestrator-tagged `CUSTOM` events. Each variant\nhas a literal `name`, so a single narrow on `chunk.name` yields a typed\n`value` with no helper or cast:\n\n```ts\nif (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'approval-requested') {\n  chunk.value.toolCallId // typed as string\n}\n```\n\nThe `StructuredOutputCompleteEvent` value is parameterized by `T`, which\nthe chat orchestrator narrows to the schema's inferred type after Standard\nSchema validation. Adapters always emit it with `T = unknown`.\n\nCaveat: tools can emit arbitrary user-defined custom events via the\n`emitCustomEvent(name, value)` context API. Those flow through the stream\nat runtime but are intentionally absent from this union — including a bare\n`CustomEvent` (whose `value: any` would poison the union) would collapse\n`chunk.value` back to `any` after the narrow. If you rely on\n`emitCustomEvent`, branch on `CUSTOM` outside the literal-`name` narrows\nor cast the chunk to `StreamChunk` to recover the wider shape.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` = `unknown`\n"}
